 provided by the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency through the Johns Hopkins Particulate Matter Research Center (RD-83241701). Funding for F.D., J.M.S., and S.L.Z. was also provided by the National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences (NIEHS) (ES012054-03) and by the NIEHS Center in Urban Environmental Health (P30 ES 03819).</p></fn></fn-group></back><floats-wrap><fig id="f1-ehp0115-000989" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>PM<sub>2.5</sub> average (&#x003bc;g/m<sup>3</sup>) for 187 U.S. counties, 2000&#x02013;2005.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ehp0115-000989f1"/></fig><fig id="f2-ehp0115-000989" position="float"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>Seasonal PM<sub>2.5</sub> averages (&#x003bc;g/m<sup>3</sup>) for 187 U.S. counties, 2000&#x02013;2005.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ehp0115-000989f2"/></fig><fig id="f3-ehp0115-000989" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Percent of PM<sub>2.5</sub> composition by component for yearly, winter, and summer averages, by region.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ehp0115-000989f3"/></fig><fig id="f4-ehp0115-000989" position="float"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>Sulfate PM<sub>2.5</sub> (&#x003bc;g/m<sup>3</sup>) averages for 187 U.S. counties, 2000&#x02013;2005.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ehp0115-000989f4"/></fig><fig id="f5-ehp0115-000989" position="float"><label>Figure 5</label><caption><p>Seasonal sulfate PM<sub>2.5</sub> (&#x003bc;g/m<sup>3</sup>) averages for 187 U.S. counties, 2000&#x02013;2005.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ehp0115-000989f5"/></fig><fig id="f6-ehp0115-000989" position="float"><label>Figure 6</label><caption><p>Nitrate PM<sub>2.5</sub> averages (&#x003bc;g/m<sup>3</sup>) for 187 U.S. counties, 2000&#x02013;2005.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ehp0115-000989f6"/></fig><fig id="f7-ehp0115-000989" position="float"><label>Figure 7</label><caption><p>Seasonal nitrate PM<sub>2.5</sub> averages (&#x003bc;g/m<sup>3</sup>) for 187 U.S. countie